  "title": "Supreme Court dismisses plea against Delhi Police's facial recognition tech and infrastructure",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court agreed to hear a plea against Delhi Police's use of facial recognition technology and biometric surveillance, citing concerns about the deployment of such measures on peaceful protesters and data privacy violations. The court also ruled against individuals involved in the Delhi riots-related protests.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court agreed to hear a plea filed by a Rajya Sabha lawmaker challenging the alleged deployment of facial recognition technology and biometric surveillance measures by Delhi Police.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court ruled against individuals involved in the Delhi riots-related protests, emphasizing concerns over data privacy and the use of such technology without proper authorization.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
