    {
      "title": "Neet stir: SC to hear plea against Delhi Police's use of facial recognition",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/neet-stir-sc-to-hear-plea-against-delhi-police-s-use-of-facial-recognition-126081300771_1.html",
      "description": "The Supreme Court on Thursday agreed to hear a plea filed by a Rajya Sabha lawmaker challenging the alleged deployment of facial recognition technology and other biometric surveillance measures by Delhi Police during the recent student protest at Jantar Mantar here.\nA bench of Chief Justice Surya Kant and Justices Joymalya Bagchi and V Mohana directed the matter be tagged with earlier petitions on the issue.\nSenior advocate Menaka Guruswamy, appearing for Rajya Sabha MP AA Rahim, said there are two issues which are a matter of concern-facial recognition of protestors done by Delhi police and data stored by private companies.\n\"One maps your face and one is a vehicle. So spectacles are used and a vehicle is also used. And that data is all taken without permission. These private entities host the data. In violation of the rules,\" she submitted.\nThe bench said it would hear the petition along with other related matters.\nRahim, who is member of the Rajya Sabha from Kerala for the Commu",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-13T07:16:54"
    }
  ]
